# diff-sentry: model roles and runtime knobs. Copy to .env; a live run needs these plus a Deno sandbox.

# --- Model roles (required for a live `pr`/`issue`/`classify` run) ---
# planner: a cheap, injection-resistant orchestrator that holds the diff in the REPL and triages.
DS_ROOT_LM=your-planner-model
# analyst: an expensive model reached via llm_query for a subtle source->sink (short questions only).
DS_SUB_LM=your-analyst-model
# One OpenAI-compatible proxy serves all roles. When DS_BASE_URL is set the model names are the plain
# ids your endpoint serves (e.g. qwen/qwen3-next), not litellm-prefixed.
DS_BASE_URL=https://your-openai-compatible-endpoint/v1
DS_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- OR: run planner + analyst on a Claude Pro/Max subscription (no API key) ---
# A role with the `claude-agent-sdk/<id>` prefix runs on your Claude subscription through the Claude
# Agent SDK (`rlm_harness.ClaudeAgentLM`, the `subscription` extra). Each call is a pure completion:
# no tools, no filesystem, no settings leakage. Prerequisites:
#   - `uv sync --extra subscription`
#   - the Claude Code CLI installed and logged in (`claude` then /login, or `claude setup-token` and
#     export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN)
#   - `unset ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`: the CLI prefers it over the subscription and would bill API credit,
#     so the adapter refuses to start while it is set
# Prefer full model ids over aliases, which drift.
#   DS_ROOT_LM=claude-agent-sdk/claude-sonnet-5     # planner on Sonnet 5
#   DS_SUB_LM=claude-agent-sdk/claude-fable-5       # analyst on Fable 5
# DS_BASE_URL/DS_API_KEY then serve only the classifier, which always needs an OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint (a subscription-only run is not supported). Set DS_CLASSIFIER_LM to a real model id (plus
# DS_CLASSIFIER_BASE_URL/DS_CLASSIFIER_API_KEY if it is a separate box). Left unset, it inherits the
# `claude-agent-sdk/…` DS_SUB_LM and config loading fails with an actionable error.
# Budgets use the same env vars as proxy mode. Each call adds ~2-5s of CLI-spawn overhead, so keep
# these runs interactive, not batch. DS_PLANNER_MAX_TOKENS has no effect here: the Agent SDK exposes
# no token or sampling controls.

# --- Second-stage classifier (the swappable seam) ---
# Defaults to the analyst model on DS_BASE_URL/DS_API_KEY. Required when the analyst runs on the
# subscription (see above).
# DS_CLASSIFIER_LM=your-strong-classifier
# DS_CLASSIFIER_BASE_URL=https://your-classifier-endpoint/v1
# DS_CLASSIFIER_API_KEY=sk-...
# DS_CLASSIFIER_CIRCUIT_BREAK=4

# --- RLM runtime ---
# DS_INTERPRETER=pyodide       # read-not-execute: the sandbox never runs the change. `deno` is an alias.
# DS_MAX_ITERATIONS=25
# DS_MAX_LLM_CALLS=8           # caps only analyst (llm_query) escalations
# DS_ADAPTER=json              # portable structured output (OpenAI + vLLM/NIM)
# DS_PLANNER_MAX_TOKENS=16384  # generous, so a reasoning planner isn't truncated to empty content

# --- Enrichment fetch (off by default: an exfil surface on attacker-authored input; GitHub-allowlisted) ---
# DS_ENABLE_FETCH=false
# DS_FETCH_ALLOW_CIDRS=198.18.0.0/16   # only if behind a fake-IP proxy / split-DNS VPN

# --- Host-side SIEM emitter (opt-in; deterministic POST after the run) ---
# DS_SIEM_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-siem/intake
# DS_SIEM_TOKEN=...
# DS_EMIT_ON=suspicious,malicious
